-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- data types: one eliminator row
-- A data type's constructor k is the value with head 100 + k and its fields as parts, a value as
-- every value is. Eliminator 3 is induction. Its arguments: the hypotheses wanted (a list, 42,
-- for each constructor a list, 42, of 0 or 1 for each field), the motive (43: none), and a branch
-- for each constructor, a function of the fields and then of a hypothesis for each field marked 1.
-- Meeting constructor k it is branch k at the fields and, for each marked field, the same
-- eliminator at that field. Nothing here names a type: which fields are of the type itself is
-- what the hypotheses' list says, and the checker holds it to the type (nk-el-ok)
nk-el-len : NkTm → Word
nk-el-len (nk-cons t r) = %wsucc (nk-el-len r)
nk-el-len t = #0
